From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 09:53:28 +0200
Subject: Do not force completion when filtering prunable inline methods
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PruneInlinedMethods is an InfoTransformer with no feature gate: its
transformInfo filters the declarations of every class denotation brought
forward past it, and the filter predicate began with symbol-flag tests, so
every declaration of every such class was completed — and merely reading
`sym.denot` replays the intervening info transforms — at whatever point the
denotation happened to advance. In the second run of a compilation-suspension
restart (a macro dependency on a -sourcepath-loaded symbol suspends the unit;
Driver.finish recompiles it in a fresh run), that reaches completers which
resolve symbols created in the first run, and compilation crashes with
StaleSymbolException. Building the Scala.js scalalib overlay
(library-js-aux with -sourcepath library/src) crashed on
scala.annotation.compileTimeOnly exactly this way; the step compiles cleanly
under -Yskip:pruneInlinedMethods,pruneInlineTraits.

isDeletable now pre-filters on the last known denotation without advancing
it: an uncompleted symbol, or one whose flags do not spell an inline method,
cannot be a specialized inline method awaiting pruning, since those are
created and completed earlier in the same run. Only genuine candidates reach
Specialization.isSpecializedMethod. Introduced upstream by #26156 (Inline
Traits & Specialized Traits); upstream candidate.

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: prunecomplete
---
 .../dotc/transform/PruneInlinedMethods.scala   | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/PruneInlinedMethods.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/PruneInlinedMethods.scala
index a630eb8cfa993636d281adf1e5fc52cc50f7338a..aeca9341dfd1eb23405d76c7300e75c03e711cdf 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/PruneInlinedMethods.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/PruneInlinedMethods.scala
@@ -41,8 +41,22 @@ class PruneInlinedMethods extends MiniPhase with InfoTransformer { thisTransform
       }
     )
 
-  private def isDeletable(sym: Symbol)(using Context): Boolean = 
-    Specialization.isSpecializedMethod(sym)
+  private def isDeletable(sym: Symbol)(using Context): Boolean =
+    // Pre-filter on the last known denotation, without advancing it: this
+    // transform runs on every class denotation brought forward past it, so an
+    // ordinary `sym.denot` access here replays the intervening info
+    // transforms and runs completers at arbitrary points — including, in the
+    // second run of a compilation-suspension restart, completers that resolve
+    // symbols of the first run, which fails with a StaleSymbolException. A
+    // symbol that is uncompleted, or not an inline method, cannot be a
+    // specialized inline method awaiting pruning (those are created and
+    // completed earlier in the same run), so only genuine candidates reach
+    // the full check.
+    val lastDenot = sym.lastKnownDenotation
+    lastDenot.isCompleted
+    && lastDenot.flagsUNSAFE.isAllOf(InlineMethod)
+    && !lastDenot.flagsUNSAFE.is(JavaDefined)
+    && Specialization.isSpecializedMethod(sym)
 }
 
 object PruneInlinedMethods {
